Description:
The architecture consists of four main loops.  The microscopic active inference layer receives partial observations from each human and updates Gaussian beliefs.  The beliefs drive individualised actions and are aggregated into a macroscopic state vector.  The macroscopic controller solves a QP at each instant to compute a global intervention that respects the CLF decrease condition, the compassion ceiling, and constitutional constraints.  The compassion bound \mathcal{C}_{\max} is computed from the state using a smooth blending function that increases the cap during crisis.  An independent memetic edge controller solves a linear program to decide which social network edges to dampen, based on harmfulness scores, ensuring the memetic reproduction number stays below unity.  All parameters (welfare weights, compassion gains, edge‑dampening thresholds) are set by human governance.

